# Cursor Rules for SaveIt Monorepo

# Monorepo Structure
- apps/web: Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Redux Toolkit)
- apps/api: FastAPI (Python 3.11+, yt-dlp, static-ffmpeg 7.0, async SSE)

# Quality Gates
- Always run `npm run lint` and ensure 0 errors.
- Always run `npm test` and ensure all Jest tests pass.
- Always run `npm run test:api` and ensure all Pytest tests pass.

# React & Next.js 16 Rules
- Do NOT call `setState` synchronously inside `useEffect` to derive state. Calculate derived values during render.
- Always escape unescaped JSX quotes (`&quot;`, `&ldquo;`, `&rdquo;`, `&apos;`).
- Maintain dark-mode zinc aesthetic with violet accents.

# Jest Testing Rules
- Always use @testing-library/react and import '@testing-library/jest-dom'.
- Always use real Redux store with configureStore.
- NEVER mock Redux store, useSelector, useDispatch, or dispatch.
- Every test file MUST include: render test, user interaction test, and Redux state verification test.
- Follow Arrange -> Act -> Assert (AAA) structure.
- Wrap components in real <Provider store={store}>.
- Prefer screen.getByRole over getByTestId.
- Mock functions must use jest.fn(), start with mock..., and be cleared in beforeEach.
- Import/define mocks before importing the component under test.

# FastAPI Rules
- Use Pydantic v2 schemas for all inputs and outputs.
- Subprocesses (yt-dlp, FFmpeg) must have timeouts and cleanup in downloads/.
